# Unified diff files must never have their line endings touched by git's
# autocrlf/eol normalization. git apply does an exact byte match against
# upstream source (LF), so a CRLF-converted copy fails every hunk that
# spans more than one context line -- exactly what broke
# tool/vendor_flutter_webrtc.ps1's `git apply` step against
# native/flutter_webrtc_eq_patch/eq_hooks.patch on any machine/runner
# with core.autocrlf=true (the common Windows default, including
# windows-latest GitHub-hosted runners). -text disables line-ending
# conversion entirely -- the safest option for a file whose line endings
# are themselves diff content, not formatting.
*.patch -text
